From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daryl Denson <9751141+denson9874@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 21:57:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/11] cheetah: ship a KernelSU Next init_boot when one is
 given

With CHEETAH_KSU_INIT_BOOT set, init_boot is that prebuilt (the build's own
init_boot patched by KernelSU Next's ksud) instead of one made from the
generic ramdisk. The build system re-signs it with the init_boot AVB key and
puts it in target-files, so the fastboot images and the OTA both carry it and
root survives updates. Unset, nothing changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 cheetah/BoardConfig.mk | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/cheetah/BoardConfig.mk b/cheetah/BoardConfig.mk
index 627e904..ec83c90 100644
--- a/cheetah/BoardConfig.mk
+++ b/cheetah/BoardConfig.mk
@@ -29,3 +29,11 @@ include $(VENDOR_PATH)/BoardConfigVendor.mk
 # AOT code after every update and run interpreted/JIT until background
 # dexopt catches up (~180 MB, well inside super).
 BOARD_USES_SYSTEM_OTHER_ODEX :=
+
+# KernelSU Next: ExpressiveOS's cheetah-images.sh builds once, patches that
+# build's init_boot with KernelSU Next (cheetah-ksu.sh), then builds again with
+# CHEETAH_KSU_INIT_BOOT set, so the images and the OTA ship the patched
+# init_boot (re-signed with our AVB key like a built one).
+ifneq ($(CHEETAH_KSU_INIT_BOOT),)
+BOARD_PREBUILT_INIT_BOOT_IMAGE := $(CHEETAH_KSU_INIT_BOOT)
+endif
